# Part 2: Working Mechanism, Architectural Layering, and Data Flow

---

## 2.1 The Architectural Layering Model

To deliver seamless connectivity without requiring hardware updates on end-user devices (smartphones, tablets, IoT sensors), the **Portable Gateway** acts as an intermediary network relay.

The system operates across three distinct operational layers:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      LOCAL ACCESS LAYER                         │
│   (Smartphones, Laptops, Wearables using Standard Wi-Fi 6 / BT)  │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ Local IP Traffic
                                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     INTELLIGENT GATEWAY LAYER                   │
│   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│   │ Network Switch Engine (Policy & Handover Manager)       │   │
│   ├────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┤   │
│   │ Terrestrial Transceiver    │  3GPP NTN Satellite Modem  │   │
│   │  (5G NR Sub-6 GHz / LTE)   │   (Band n255 / n256 RF)    │   │
│   └────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┘   │
└────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ Uplink / Downlink
                                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    SPACE & CORE NETWORK LAYER                   │
│      (LEO Satellites ➔ Earth Gateways ➔ 5G Core Network)        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

```

1. **Local Access Layer (Short-Range):** The gateway functions as a low-power, high-efficiency Wi-Fi Access Point (AP). It handles local IP assignment, packet aggregation, and authentication for user devices.
2. **Intelligent Gateway Layer (Core Switch Engine):** The processing brain of the device. It dynamically assesses link quality, power budgets, and terrestrial network availability to decide how packet traffic should exit the device.
3. **Space & Core Network Layer (Global Backhaul):** The long-range transport layer. It routes packets over standard 5G cell towers when available, or translates them into 3GPP Non-Terrestrial Network (NTN) signals directed at Low Earth Orbit (LEO) satellite constellations.

