## 2.2 Protocol Stack Mapping: The Universal Protocol Translator

The core engineering breakthrough of this gateway is its **dual-stack protocol translation engine**. The gateway receives standard TCP/IP traffic over IEEE 802.11 (Wi-Fi) from the user's phone, encapsulating and converting it into a 3GPP 5G NR-NTN protocol stack on the satellite interface.

```
[ User Smartphone ]             [ Portable Gateway Translator ]         [ LEO Satellite System ]
┌─────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────────────┐         ┌──────────────────────┐
│  Applications   │             │                             │         │                      │
├─────────────────┤             ├──────────────┬──────────────┤         ├──────────────────────┤
│    TCP / IP     ├────────────►│   TCP / IP   │ SDAP / PDCP  ├────────►│ 5G Core Network Data │
├─────────────────┤             ├──────────────┼──────────────┤         ├──────────────────────┤
│  802.11 MAC     ├────────────►│  802.11 MAC  │  RLC / MAC   ├────────►│ 3GPP Satellite MAC   │
├─────────────────┤             ├──────────────┼──────────────┤         ├──────────────────────┤
│ Wi-Fi PHY Radio ├────────────►│  Wi-Fi PHY   │ NTN PHY RF   ├────────►│ Space Band n255/n256 │
└─────────────────┘             └──────────────┴──────────────┘         └──────────────────────┘
  (Standard Wi-Fi Link)                                                    (Global Space Link)

```

### Protocol Conversion Breakdown:

* **Service Data Adaptation Protocol (SDAP):** Maps user-plane Quality of Service (QoS) flows directly to specific data radio bearers (DRBs). Emergency messages and voice calls receive higher priority queuing over background data.
* **Packet Data Convergence Protocol (PDCP):** Manages IP header compression (ROHC), ciphering, and packet reordering. In satellite links where latency fluctuates, PDCP prevents packet drops.
* **Radio Link Control (RLC) & MAC Layers:** Adapted under 3GPP Release 17/18 specs to extend timer thresholds (e.g., `t-Reassembly` and HARQ retransmission timers) to prevent false packet-loss dropouts caused by long space distances.
* **NTN Physical (PHY) Layer:** Modulates data using OFDMA waveforms tailored for space, incorporating GNSS (GPS) assisted Doppler shift pre-compensation before transmitting up to the satellite.

